1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:01,269
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:01,294 --> 00:00:02,307
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:02,332 --> 00:00:03,415
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,466
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,491 --> 00:00:05,760
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:01:07,168 --> 00:01:08,737
Is it a series about golf?

7
00:01:08,762 --> 00:01:11,526
Would it end up
feeling like a documentary?

8
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:13,805
Would it appeal to
a wider audience?

9
00:01:13,830 --> 00:01:15,359
It really introduces you to golf,

10
00:01:15,384 --> 00:01:18,209
and you get so many different
experiences from just one series.

11
00:01:18,234 --> 00:01:20,464
It's not just about golf.
I promise it's a lot of fun.

12
00:01:20,515 --> 00:01:25,253
The golf course looked
way better than I ever expected.

13
00:01:25,305 --> 00:01:27,371
It was just...
absolutely beautiful.

14
00:01:27,396 --> 00:01:29,991
I was like, "Really? Is that
the same course we played on?"

15
00:01:30,016 --> 00:01:33,325
But in the end,
the way the script turned out,

16
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:36,584
it made golf feel like
a part of everyday life.

17
00:01:36,682 --> 00:01:38,529
Even while I was on set,
I kept thinking,

18
00:01:38,594 --> 00:01:43,990
"Why golf? What made us
want to tell a story about golf?"

19
00:01:47,078 --> 00:01:48,819
Hello!

20
00:01:48,925 --> 00:01:52,386
- We're the cast of...
- Fairway of Love!

21
00:01:52,546 --> 00:01:54,747
I'm Ing Tanatcha Devahastin.

22
00:01:54,772 --> 00:01:58,001
I play Pro Venus.

23
00:01:58,171 --> 00:02:00,577
Hi, I'm Cartoon
Kittaya Iemnopmanee.

24
00:02:00,602 --> 00:02:02,742
I play Nana.

25
00:02:02,766 --> 00:02:04,827
I'm Bam Rinrada Wisutthiareeruk.

26
00:02:04,852 --> 00:02:06,129
I play Belle.

27
00:02:06,154 --> 00:02:08,067
I'm Minagi Warisaya Boonyatap.

28
00:02:08,092 --> 00:02:09,426
I play Pro Jin.

29
00:02:09,451 --> 00:02:13,435
It all started with Ninee,
our executive producer.

30
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:16,694
She brought up the idea
of doing a GL project

31
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:19,753
and combining GL
with some kind of sport.

32
00:02:19,778 --> 00:02:21,009
So, what sport should it be?

33
00:02:21,034 --> 00:02:22,597
Then she asked,

34
00:02:22,622 --> 00:02:27,982
"Could we make a GL series
centered around golf?"

35
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:30,795
Golf is a sport where you have to
keep moving forward.

36
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:34,458
If you hit a bad shot,
you can't dwell on it forever.

37
00:02:34,483 --> 00:02:36,624
You have to keep moving forward.

38
00:02:36,649 --> 00:02:40,937
With every shot,
you just keep moving forward.

39
00:02:40,962 --> 00:02:43,831
When I first heard it was
about golf, my first thought was,

40
00:02:43,856 --> 00:02:45,843
"Am I gonna have to play golf?"

41
00:02:45,868 --> 00:02:47,930
But then I found out
I'd be playing a secretary,

42
00:02:47,955 --> 00:02:49,542
and I was like,
"Okay, what a relief.

43
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:51,147
I'm the only one
who got away with it!"

44
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:53,725
She was on the team that launched
our mining project in...

45
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,150
where was it again?
(Take 1)

46
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:56,225
Ranong.

47
00:02:58,177 --> 00:02:59,511
Damn it, same mistake.

48
00:02:59,535 --> 00:03:01,920
"I assigned Belle to be your
assistant." You missed a bit.

49
00:03:03,039 --> 00:03:05,030
I assigned Belle
to be your advisor...

50
00:03:05,054 --> 00:03:06,078
Was it "advisor"?
(Take 2)

51
00:03:06,508 --> 00:03:07,873
- Assistant.
- Assistant.

52
00:03:10,559 --> 00:03:12,981
I assigned Belle
to be your assistant.

53
00:03:13,113 --> 00:03:16,310
She was on the team that launched
our mining project in Ranong.

54
00:03:16,335 --> 00:03:17,965
Now that it's up and running,

55
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:19,576
I brought her here to help you.

56
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:23,423
Where did you just say it was?
Ranong?

57
00:03:24,774 --> 00:03:26,774
Maybe just stick with Rayong.

58
00:03:27,098 --> 00:03:28,942
But we've already gone
Ranong, Rayong...

59
00:03:28,967 --> 00:03:30,045
Yala!

60
00:03:30,605 --> 00:03:33,019
This was my first acting role,
(First role with a veteran!)

61
00:03:33,044 --> 00:03:35,020
and I had to work with Am.

62
00:03:35,045 --> 00:03:36,846
At first, I was so nervous
I'd mess up.

63
00:03:36,871 --> 00:03:38,180
And I did, plenty of times.

64
00:03:38,205 --> 00:03:40,291
I kept talking too fast
and rushing my lines.

65
00:03:40,316 --> 00:03:42,957
Ta, our acting coach, would be,
"I can't understand a word!"

66
00:03:42,982 --> 00:03:44,382
But Am was really sweet about it.

67
00:03:44,407 --> 00:03:47,869
We kept getting stuck on
that mining line.

68
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:49,697
Ranong, Rayong, Yala...
for like ten takes.

69
00:03:49,722 --> 00:03:53,260
I feel like he was actually
trying to help me out,

70
00:03:53,285 --> 00:03:55,884
keeping the atmosphere light

71
00:03:55,909 --> 00:04:00,079
so I could relax
and perform more naturally.

72
00:04:00,157 --> 00:04:03,930
When we met him,
Am was always chatting with us.

73
00:04:03,955 --> 00:04:06,058
- He has a daughter too, Ally.
- Right.

74
00:04:06,083 --> 00:04:08,282
And he was just so nice to us.

75
00:04:08,307 --> 00:04:11,037
He'd talk to us a lot
and was really supportive.

76
00:04:11,062 --> 00:04:12,521
He was always
encouraging us, like,

77
00:04:12,546 --> 00:04:14,550
"You're doing great!
Such a trooper!"

78
00:04:14,575 --> 00:04:16,658
So we never felt nervous
acting with him.

79
00:04:16,683 --> 00:04:18,905
And he is such a professional.

80
00:04:18,930 --> 00:04:20,429
It made acting with him
really fun,

81
00:04:20,453 --> 00:04:23,858
especially when he'd improvise
and we'd get to play off him.

82
00:04:24,703 --> 00:04:27,203
(Fully committed to every role!)

83
00:04:35,774 --> 00:04:38,305
Since the series was about golf,
we were told,

84
00:04:38,330 --> 00:04:40,537
"You should start
taking golf lessons."

85
00:04:40,562 --> 00:04:43,935
But I had no idea I'd actually
be playing a golf pro.

86
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:46,295
Then when I found out
I was playing one, I was like...

87
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:48,657
"Okay, time to get serious."

88
00:04:48,682 --> 00:04:53,799
These days, we're seeing
a lot more women playing golf.

89
00:04:53,946 --> 00:04:58,130
And there's a certain elegance
to women's golf,

90
00:04:58,155 --> 00:05:01,684
especially when it comes to
the fashion and what they wear.

91
00:05:01,709 --> 00:05:07,307
So we thought those two elements
could really come together,

92
00:05:07,332 --> 00:05:10,477
and work really well together.

93
00:05:10,502 --> 00:05:15,807
It's a sport that promotes
both health and beauty,

94
00:05:15,832 --> 00:05:18,350
while also being entertaining.

95
00:05:19,683 --> 00:05:22,776
Welcome back, Miss Nana,
all the way from Paris,

96
00:05:22,801 --> 00:05:26,731
- to Bangkok City, Thailand!
- Yay!

97
00:05:26,834 --> 00:05:29,731
(What are your characters like?)

98
00:05:29,756 --> 00:05:31,934
At first glance,
she might seem a little spoiled.

99
00:05:31,959 --> 00:05:34,690
But really, she's just
very confident in herself.

100
00:05:34,715 --> 00:05:36,420
She knows what she wants,

101
00:05:36,445 --> 00:05:39,321
and believes that what
she's doing is for the best.

102
00:05:39,346 --> 00:05:40,946
So she may come across
as spoiled,

103
00:05:40,971 --> 00:05:43,066
but she's actually
very open to listening to others.

104
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:50,300
Dad!

105
00:05:50,324 --> 00:05:54,769
Pro Vee is actually
a really talented golfer.

106
00:05:54,794 --> 00:05:57,540
She used to win tournaments
all the time as a kid.

107
00:05:57,565 --> 00:06:01,497
But then something happened
that left a lasting scar on her.

108
00:06:01,522 --> 00:06:03,411
So she became
a teaching pro instead.

109
00:06:03,436 --> 00:06:05,834
And because she really wants
her students to do well,

110
00:06:05,859 --> 00:06:08,573
she can be a little strict.
(Trying to play it cool!)

111
00:06:08,598 --> 00:06:11,425
On the outside,
she can seem pretty stoic.

112
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:14,625
Just like me, actually! Stoic on
the outside, but a softie inside.

113
00:06:14,650 --> 00:06:16,580
The characters
we originally envisioned

114
00:06:16,605 --> 00:06:18,438
and the actors
we ended up casting

115
00:06:18,462 --> 00:06:20,125
are actually very similar.

116
00:06:20,150 --> 00:06:25,096
Belle is hardworking
and really good at what she does.

117
00:06:25,121 --> 00:06:27,384
Whenever there's a new project,

118
00:06:27,409 --> 00:06:30,103
the Chairman sends Belle in first

119
00:06:30,128 --> 00:06:32,308
to test the waters
and help get things started.

120
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:34,758
Then when his daughter
comes back from France

121
00:06:34,783 --> 00:06:36,138
to take over the golf course,

122
00:06:36,162 --> 00:06:38,767
Belle is put in charge
of looking after Miss Nana

123
00:06:38,792 --> 00:06:41,596
and taking care of
whatever she needs.

124
00:06:41,954 --> 00:06:44,866
That thing I asked you
to look into...

125
00:06:44,891 --> 00:06:45,938
I was right, wasn't I?

126
00:06:51,861 --> 00:06:52,883
I knew it.

127
00:06:56,762 --> 00:06:58,349
What do you want to do next,
Miss Nana?

128
00:06:58,624 --> 00:07:04,276
Pro Jin is the quiet, cool type.
She doesn't talk much.

129
00:07:04,301 --> 00:07:08,833
She starts out as a golf pro
at The Royal Green,

130
00:07:08,858 --> 00:07:12,828
then gets the chance to move to
Good View, where she meets Belle

131
00:07:12,853 --> 00:07:16,513
and faces her old rival, Pro Vee.
(Finds both romance and rivalry!)

132
00:07:16,538 --> 00:07:20,764
It matched my vision
even better than expected.

133
00:07:20,789 --> 00:07:22,780
Women's golf
is really nice to watch.

134
00:07:22,805 --> 00:07:25,392
The way they swing,
it's so graceful.

135
00:07:25,417 --> 00:07:29,228
There's just so much about it
that's visually appealing.

136
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:43,912
Food's here! Food's here!

137
00:07:43,937 --> 00:07:46,049
Here you go!

138
00:07:46,074 --> 00:07:47,796
This happened all the time.

139
00:07:47,821 --> 00:07:51,458
I should explain what it's like
doing a scene with Pingpong.

140
00:07:51,483 --> 00:07:53,896
On the first take, you never know
what to expect.

141
00:07:53,921 --> 00:07:55,603
You're like,
"What's she gonna do?"

142
00:07:55,628 --> 00:07:57,774
She always improvises,
(Basically just being herself!)

143
00:07:57,799 --> 00:07:59,857
and it's absolutely hilarious.

144
00:07:59,882 --> 00:08:02,585
So then you're like, "I know
what she's gonna do now."

145
00:08:02,610 --> 00:08:05,222
"I'll keep a straight face
on take two."

146
00:08:05,247 --> 00:08:06,573
Nope! Because guess what?

147
00:08:06,598 --> 00:08:08,271
She does something
completely different.

148
00:08:08,886 --> 00:08:10,368
She never does
the same thing twice.

149
00:08:10,393 --> 00:08:13,260
So just when you think,
"Okay, I can handle her now,"

150
00:08:13,285 --> 00:08:14,863
take two comes around... nope!

151
00:08:14,888 --> 00:08:17,522
Even Am couldn't keep
a straight face. Remember?

152
00:08:17,547 --> 00:08:20,025
- Yeah, I remember.
- There was this one scene,

153
00:08:20,050 --> 00:08:22,203
even Am couldn't stop himself
from laughing.

154
00:08:22,228 --> 00:08:23,648
So what chance did I have?

155
00:08:25,014 --> 00:08:27,991
- Delicious, right?
- Super delicious!

156
00:08:28,370 --> 00:08:30,981
No, no.
You have to say it like this.

157
00:08:31,602 --> 00:08:34,601
"De-li-cious!"
Come on, say it!

158
00:08:35,605 --> 00:08:36,970
De-li-cious!

159
00:08:37,928 --> 00:08:41,800
That's it! You gotta drag it out,
Miss Nana. One... two... three!

160
00:08:42,223 --> 00:08:44,581
- De-li-cious!
- De-li-cious! Yay!

161
00:08:44,606 --> 00:08:47,258
Pingpong is another cast member

162
00:08:47,283 --> 00:08:49,166
who brings so much color
to the show.

163
00:08:49,190 --> 00:08:52,532
She takes the series
and the fun to another level.

164
00:08:52,557 --> 00:08:55,574
She even brings up
the energy on set.

165
00:08:55,599 --> 00:09:00,379
Plus, the younger actors
get to learn so much from her.

166
00:09:00,411 --> 00:09:03,106
Pingpong didn't even learn
my name until the very last day.

167
00:09:03,131 --> 00:09:05,798
- The last day of filming?
- Yeah! But before that...

168
00:09:05,823 --> 00:09:10,665
I was the one she'd always
chat with in the dressing room.

169
00:09:10,824 --> 00:09:14,138
Just zoning out all day.
Like this.

170
00:09:20,724 --> 00:09:22,247
But this kitchen taught me

171
00:09:22,981 --> 00:09:27,337
an important lesson every time
I reached for a cashew.

172
00:09:27,490 --> 00:09:30,163
If it's for sale,
don't just help yourself!

173
00:09:30,687 --> 00:09:33,614
I snuck about two during a scene.
(Caught sneaking a bite on set!)

174
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:37,261
Two cashews, five baht.
That's 2.50 each!

175
00:09:39,132 --> 00:09:40,551
(A nice big bite!)

176
00:09:40,575 --> 00:09:42,516
The moment
Pingpong walks onto set,

177
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:46,205
everything just gets brighter,
more colorful and more lively.

178
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:48,375
She has so much energy,

179
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,920
and it naturally rubs off
on everyone around her.

180
00:09:50,945 --> 00:09:52,288
(Pingpong = the life of the set!)

181
00:09:52,312 --> 00:09:53,872
She doesn't even
do it on purpose.

182
00:09:53,897 --> 00:09:56,325
Everyone just
picks up on her energy.

183
00:09:56,370 --> 00:10:00,457
Whenever she shows up,
you hear all this chatter.

184
00:10:00,482 --> 00:10:04,987
A set that was totally quiet
suddenly comes alive.

185
00:10:05,012 --> 00:10:06,405
No question about it.

186
00:10:06,430 --> 00:10:08,563
Pingpong takes
the number one spot for me.

187
00:10:08,762 --> 00:10:10,125
Whenever this character appears,

188
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:12,436
you know there'll be
smiles and laughter.

189
00:10:12,461 --> 00:10:15,068
We wanted Chef Queen
to be a character

190
00:10:15,093 --> 00:10:17,554
who ties everything together
at the golf course.

191
00:10:17,579 --> 00:10:20,465
She has known Miss Nana
since Nana was a child,

192
00:10:20,490 --> 00:10:26,104
and she always tries to be there
and support her however she can.

193
00:10:26,129 --> 00:10:27,971
She brings
a lot of light to the story

194
00:10:27,996 --> 00:10:30,677
and gives us
plenty of smiles and laughs.

195
00:10:30,702 --> 00:10:32,812
So we really have
Pingpong to thank

196
00:10:32,844 --> 00:10:34,777
for bringing so much color
to the series.

197
00:10:40,135 --> 00:10:44,294
We thought a lot about
how to tell the story

198
00:10:44,319 --> 00:10:47,625
without making golf feel boring

199
00:10:47,650 --> 00:10:50,465
or forcing too much of it
on the audience.

200
00:10:50,490 --> 00:10:53,076
Some people already love golf.

201
00:10:53,101 --> 00:10:55,445
Some are
pretty indifferent to it,

202
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:57,033
and some
aren't interested at all.

203
00:10:57,058 --> 00:11:00,425
So how do we make
the series enjoyable for people

204
00:11:00,450 --> 00:11:02,475
who already know golf
without boring them?

205
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:04,658
The story itself
has to be fun too.

206
00:11:04,695 --> 00:11:07,964
Help! Somebody help!
There's a thief!

207
00:11:07,989 --> 00:11:09,154
- What the hell?
- A thief!

208
00:11:11,129 --> 00:11:16,136
Then there are people who aren't
into golf at all, but love GL.

209
00:11:16,161 --> 00:11:18,389
So we had to figure out

210
00:11:18,414 --> 00:11:22,177
how to blend GL and golf
in a way that feels natural.

211
00:11:22,202 --> 00:11:26,426
Everything we put into the series
is grounded in reality,

212
00:11:26,514 --> 00:11:28,836
whether it's something
from the world of golf

213
00:11:28,861 --> 00:11:31,225
or something
that happens in real life.

214
00:11:31,250 --> 00:11:34,741
If you watch our series,
Fairway of Love,

215
00:11:34,766 --> 00:11:38,762
you'll see that in every shot,
every episode, every scene,

216
00:11:38,787 --> 00:11:42,258
everything you see
could actually happen.

217
00:11:42,389 --> 00:11:45,332
Nothing is too over-the-top.

218
00:11:52,849 --> 00:11:57,257
The crew put so much into this,
every single department.

219
00:11:57,373 --> 00:12:03,409
Lighting, sound, camera,
photography. Everyone.

220
00:12:03,434 --> 00:12:07,332
Everyone was so thorough,
even before filming began.

221
00:12:07,357 --> 00:12:11,290
Golf isn't something everyone is
already familiar with,

222
00:12:11,408 --> 00:12:13,839
so everyone did
a ton of homework.

223
00:12:20,674 --> 00:12:25,183
The sun and the heat
were obviously a challenge.

224
00:12:25,208 --> 00:12:26,979
When you're out in the sun,

225
00:12:27,003 --> 00:12:30,784
there's the sweat
and everything else to deal with.

226
00:12:40,578 --> 00:12:46,019
And shooting outdoors
in such open spaces,

227
00:12:46,044 --> 00:12:49,572
there were so many things
that were hard to control.

228
00:12:49,597 --> 00:12:53,418
But we still had to
keep everything

229
00:12:53,443 --> 00:12:57,445
as close to our planned workflow
as possible.

230
00:13:45,712 --> 00:13:46,720
Romantic, huh?

231
00:13:46,934 --> 00:13:49,952
- At least finish the song!
- That's all I know!

232
00:13:50,515 --> 00:13:52,379
I'm kind of paranoid about this.
I get nervous.

233
00:13:52,404 --> 00:13:55,286
Whenever I play golf, I feel like
everyone's watching me.

234
00:13:55,311 --> 00:13:58,232
At the driving range,
no one's really watching you.

235
00:13:58,257 --> 00:14:01,005
But in my head, "Everyone's
watching. I have to do well!"

236
00:14:01,030 --> 00:14:03,195
And the more I get into
my own head and can't relax,

237
00:14:03,220 --> 00:14:06,359
the worse I play. I have to
just loosen up and swing.

238
00:14:06,384 --> 00:14:09,614
But on set, it's even worse.
"5, 4, 3, 2... action!"

239
00:14:09,639 --> 00:14:11,982
"When I give you the cue,
go ahead and swing, Ing."

240
00:14:12,007 --> 00:14:13,205
Wait for the cue.

241
00:14:16,948 --> 00:14:18,509
And... action!

242
00:14:22,598 --> 00:14:25,260
- Set!
- And... action!

243
00:14:25,475 --> 00:14:27,973
Do you see what I mean?
It's so much pressure!

244
00:14:27,998 --> 00:14:30,026
- So much pressure.
- "Now? I have to hit it now?"

245
00:14:30,051 --> 00:14:32,413
When mentally,
I'm not even ready yet.

246
00:14:32,438 --> 00:14:33,781
So I found it really hard.

247
00:14:33,805 --> 00:14:37,055
Even crying scenes and
dramatic scenes aren't this hard.

248
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:39,778
Seriously, hitting a golf ball
on camera is the hardest thing.

249
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:42,185
I got lucky. I didn't
have to be that good at golf.

250
00:14:42,210 --> 00:14:44,336
I had to know how to play,
just not at her level.

251
00:14:44,361 --> 00:14:45,952
Right, but my swing
had to look good,

252
00:14:45,977 --> 00:14:47,993
with that little club twirl
at the end.

253
00:14:48,017 --> 00:14:50,605
And in the pilot, you might've
noticed when I twirled it...

254
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:52,131
It got stuck.

255
00:14:52,155 --> 00:14:53,576
And they didn't even cut it out!

256
00:14:53,896 --> 00:14:56,569
- It's fine. Nobody noticed.
- But it's okay. I looked pretty!

257
00:14:56,594 --> 00:14:58,651
If you pay close attention,

258
00:14:58,676 --> 00:15:02,019
you can actually see how much
the actors improved at golf.

259
00:15:02,044 --> 00:15:04,107
As you watch, you start to notice
the little details

260
00:15:04,132 --> 00:15:06,076
that make you think,
"Oh, she really is a pro."

261
00:15:06,101 --> 00:15:09,543
You get a sense of how much
training a pro goes through.

262
00:15:09,568 --> 00:15:13,579
It almost feels like

263
00:15:13,604 --> 00:15:17,515
we got a little taste of
being golf pros ourselves.

264
00:15:17,621 --> 00:15:24,181
We also have real female
golf pros in the series.

265
00:15:24,282 --> 00:15:31,113
We wanted to help open a path
for athletes into entertainment

266
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:35,187
and bring something authentic
and true to life into the series.

267
00:15:35,267 --> 00:15:38,564
We wanted to show golf
from an outsider's perspective,

268
00:15:38,589 --> 00:15:40,304
then gradually learns about it

269
00:15:40,329 --> 00:15:42,329
and discovers
how much fun it can be.

270
00:15:42,354 --> 00:15:44,553
Golf isn't some exclusive sport.

271
00:15:44,578 --> 00:15:47,325
It's something anyone can enjoy.
(Golf is for everyone!)

272
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:50,255
I wanted to try something new.

273
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:54,069
Most of the series and dramas
I've worked on before

274
00:15:54,094 --> 00:15:57,597
have been
pretty dark and dramatic,

275
00:15:57,622 --> 00:16:01,984
usually with a lot of
heavy, intense storylines.

276
00:16:02,009 --> 00:16:07,115
So I also wanted to prove to
myself that I could tell a story

277
00:16:07,140 --> 00:16:10,127
where the characters'
warmth and charm

278
00:16:10,152 --> 00:16:12,049
could simply make people smile.

279
00:16:12,073 --> 00:16:14,542
- A stomach marches on its army.
- Huh?

280
00:16:14,986 --> 00:16:16,669
You know, an army marches.

281
00:16:16,702 --> 00:16:19,253
If you're going to work hard,
you need to eat first.

282
00:16:19,278 --> 00:16:22,516
"An army marches on its stomach."
At least get the saying right.

283
00:16:23,556 --> 00:16:26,282
For the viewers, pay close
attention to Cartoon's acting.

284
00:16:26,307 --> 00:16:28,054
I was really impressed by it.

285
00:16:28,079 --> 00:16:30,897
She has this playful,
childlike side,

286
00:16:30,922 --> 00:16:33,636
but then there's another
side of her that's serious

287
00:16:33,661 --> 00:16:36,202
and has to step up
as an executive.

288
00:16:36,227 --> 00:16:39,425
We get to see Cartoon's ambition

289
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:43,132
and her determination to
overcome whatever comes her way.

290
00:16:43,157 --> 00:16:45,212
We get to see
so many different layers

291
00:16:45,237 --> 00:16:48,637
to Cartoon's performance
as Miss Nana.

292
00:16:48,662 --> 00:16:50,225
If you watch closely,
you'll notice...

293
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:54,844
how Cartoon switches gears
depending on the situation,

294
00:16:54,869 --> 00:16:58,097
and which version of Miss Nana
she brings out in each moment.

295
00:16:58,122 --> 00:17:00,237
And she makes
those choices really well.

296
00:17:08,793 --> 00:17:10,900
Bank is honestly so sweet.

297
00:17:10,925 --> 00:17:14,750
Whenever we were about to shoot,
he'd be so full of energy.

298
00:17:14,775 --> 00:17:17,414
He'd practically sprint onto set.

299
00:17:17,439 --> 00:17:20,490
It was really cute. He really
gave this project his all.

300
00:17:20,515 --> 00:17:21,872
- Absolutely.
- Yeah.

301
00:17:21,897 --> 00:17:24,135
I heard this was
his first series too.

302
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:28,986
So in a way,
we were both newbies together.

303
00:17:29,011 --> 00:17:31,831
I'm really glad we got to
have him as our director.

304
00:17:31,888 --> 00:17:37,807
I actually preferred explaining
things to the actors myself,

305
00:17:37,832 --> 00:17:40,770
because everything was new.

306
00:17:40,795 --> 00:17:45,852
If I gave notes over the radio
or through an assistant,

307
00:17:45,877 --> 00:17:49,530
what got passed along
might not be exactly

308
00:17:49,555 --> 00:17:53,220
what I meant or wanted.

309
00:17:53,245 --> 00:17:55,133
You turn around,
and just as she comes out,

310
00:17:55,158 --> 00:17:57,158
you get startled
and quickly duck away.

311
00:17:57,483 --> 00:17:59,943
- Oh, okay.
- Then once she walks away...

312
00:18:05,632 --> 00:18:08,819
- Like this?
- Yeah. You don't need to...

313
00:18:10,361 --> 00:18:12,131
And... action!

314
00:18:39,346 --> 00:18:42,063
(The ship of the set.)

315
00:18:42,150 --> 00:18:45,342
The director
and assistant director!

316
00:18:46,392 --> 00:18:48,154
Bank and Arm.

317
00:18:48,218 --> 00:18:53,555
I'd sit behind the monitors.
There'd be Bank, Arm and Ta,

318
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:56,297
and I'd be sitting right
behind them.

319
00:18:56,322 --> 00:18:59,466
So I got to see
all the little interactions

320
00:18:59,491 --> 00:19:02,758
between our director
and assistant director.

321
00:19:02,783 --> 00:19:06,175
Whenever something
went wrong on set,

322
00:19:06,200 --> 00:19:08,460
they'd immediately work together
to sort it out.

323
00:19:08,485 --> 00:19:12,005
And whenever we shot
a beautiful or romantic scene,

324
00:19:12,030 --> 00:19:16,224
you could see them getting
into it too, looking so happy.

325
00:19:16,249 --> 00:19:19,362
And they're two guys, you know?

326
00:19:19,387 --> 00:19:22,891
Two very manly guys, at that!

327
00:19:22,930 --> 00:19:28,177
Since it's a GL series,
we had a lot of women on set.

328
00:19:28,202 --> 00:19:30,569
And we had another assistant
named Arm.

329
00:19:30,594 --> 00:19:33,712
He became my partner in crime.

330
00:19:33,737 --> 00:19:35,382
That's the right word, right?
"Partner"?

331
00:19:35,407 --> 00:19:39,513
Whenever we had
to demonstrate something

332
00:19:39,538 --> 00:19:43,382
or block out a scene together,
it wouldn't really be appropriate

333
00:19:43,407 --> 00:19:45,725
to pull one of the women in,
so I'd grab Arm instead.

334
00:19:45,750 --> 00:19:48,696
And sometimes we'd have to
get pretty close,

335
00:19:48,737 --> 00:19:53,866
so the crew on set
would tease us about it.

336
00:19:54,059 --> 00:19:55,098
The chemistry!

337
00:19:55,123 --> 00:19:56,886
You should see him
behind the monitors.

338
00:19:56,911 --> 00:20:00,085
In front of everyone, he acts
all serious and director-like.

339
00:20:00,110 --> 00:20:01,611
So what's he like
behind the monitors?

340
00:20:01,636 --> 00:20:03,708
When he gets the shot he wants,
first he goes...

341
00:20:04,142 --> 00:20:06,942
Then he starts stomping his feet,
giggling away like this!

342
00:20:06,967 --> 00:20:09,620
I don't think
he even turned his radio off!

343
00:20:19,753 --> 00:20:20,824
Cut!

344
00:21:12,248 --> 00:21:15,555
Overall, everything
went really well.

345
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:18,042
The younger cast
were all wonderful.

346
00:21:18,067 --> 00:21:21,649
They delivered exactly
what we'd hoped for.

347
00:21:21,674 --> 00:21:26,066
I hope Fairway of Love

348
00:21:26,091 --> 00:21:28,719
will have everyone smiling
along with the characters

349
00:21:28,744 --> 00:21:35,326
and with the story
we can't wait to share with you.

350
00:21:42,259 --> 00:21:45,462
How often do you clean your room?

351
00:21:45,830 --> 00:21:48,203
Every day? Every other day?
Once a week?

352
00:21:49,035 --> 00:21:51,961
It varies,
but I never let it get messy.

353
00:21:53,257 --> 00:21:55,148
Current relationship status...

354
00:21:55,173 --> 00:21:59,818
Single, married, divorced,
talking to someone...

355
00:21:59,843 --> 00:22:01,878
or secretly got yourself
a golden retriever?

356
00:22:02,353 --> 00:22:03,393
Single.

357
00:22:04,179 --> 00:22:09,057
Last question. Pro Jin,
what makes a woman beautiful?

358
00:22:11,199 --> 00:22:13,975
Her mind.

359
00:22:35,634 --> 00:22:38,874
I have Pro Jin to thank
for making me speak more clearly.

360
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,906
Right, you had to learn
to open your mouth wider.

361
00:22:40,931 --> 00:22:42,708
Yeah. I tend to
barely open my mouth.

362
00:22:42,732 --> 00:22:45,565
I was scared I'd mess up my lines
And I did, plenty of times.

363
00:22:45,590 --> 00:22:48,277
I kept talking too fast
and rushing my lines.

364
00:22:48,302 --> 00:22:51,046
Whenever there was a scene
we didn't quite understand,

365
00:22:51,071 --> 00:22:53,071
Coach Ta would clarify it.

366
00:22:53,096 --> 00:22:56,581
he'd say, "Ing, if you went
through what Pro Vee did,

367
00:22:56,606 --> 00:23:00,319
or if you were Pro Vee right now,
what would you do?"

368
00:23:00,344 --> 00:23:02,732
Whenever we had a tough scene,
Coach Ta would step right in

369
00:23:02,757 --> 00:23:05,934
and walk us through
the character, step by step.

370
00:23:05,959 --> 00:23:08,450
And once he'd finished and we
were about to go into the scene,

371
00:23:08,475 --> 00:23:11,444
he'd always go, "You can do it.
I know you can, Toon!"

372
00:23:11,469 --> 00:23:13,819
Thank you so much
for always encouraging us.

373
00:23:25,050 --> 00:23:29,852
Ing is beautiful, cool,
and really smart.

374
00:23:30,027 --> 00:23:33,517
So when she became Pro Vee,
it was a perfect match.

375
00:23:33,542 --> 00:23:35,678
She has
this natural strength to her,

376
00:23:35,703 --> 00:23:38,411
while still being
very feminine and beautiful.

377
00:23:38,514 --> 00:23:41,544
And just like her character,

378
00:23:41,569 --> 00:23:43,953
she's naturally quiet,
cool and composed.

379
00:23:43,978 --> 00:23:49,415
Whenever we gave her direction
or asked her to try something,

380
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:53,945
she was able to give us
exactly what we were looking for.

381
00:23:53,970 --> 00:24:00,544
I think Ing has
a real natural talent for acting.

382
00:24:00,569 --> 00:24:03,358
I think she can go really far.

383
00:24:03,383 --> 00:24:05,168
Ing was lucky

384
00:24:05,192 --> 00:24:07,505
because she was already
quite similar to her character.

385
00:24:07,530 --> 00:24:09,212
She already had
some experience with golf.

386
00:24:09,237 --> 00:24:12,191
When we first saw Ing
in her golf-pro look,

387
00:24:12,216 --> 00:24:15,430
we immediately thought,
she could totally be a golf pro.

388
00:24:15,455 --> 00:24:17,465
But when it comes to
actual skill,

389
00:24:17,490 --> 00:24:19,063
there's a pretty big gap

390
00:24:19,087 --> 00:24:21,078
between knowing how to play
and being a pro.

391
00:24:21,103 --> 00:24:24,750
So Ing put in a lot of work
to make people believe that...

392
00:24:24,775 --> 00:24:26,357
she didn't just know
how to play golf,

393
00:24:26,381 --> 00:24:28,162
she was a professional golfer.

394
00:24:28,187 --> 00:24:30,544
With her confidence
and the look in her eyes,

395
00:24:30,569 --> 00:24:34,035
we could really believe
she was a golf pro.

396
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:38,374
As for Cartoon,
I'd have to call her...

397
00:24:38,399 --> 00:24:42,121
my little wonder girl.

398
00:24:42,146 --> 00:24:45,532
The wonder girl
of Fairway of Love.

399
00:24:45,557 --> 00:24:48,685
I honestly didn't expect her

400
00:24:48,710 --> 00:24:53,449
to be this incredibly adorable!

401
00:24:53,511 --> 00:24:56,503
Whether she's being cute or sad,

402
00:24:56,528 --> 00:25:01,101
in a lighthearted scene
or something more serious,

403
00:25:01,126 --> 00:25:06,091
Cartoon expresses emotion so well
through her face and eyes.

404
00:25:06,116 --> 00:25:09,596
Her body language
is also incredibly expressive.

405
00:25:09,921 --> 00:25:14,146
This is Cartoon's first time
in a leading role,

406
00:25:14,171 --> 00:25:16,303
and she did such a great job.

407
00:25:16,328 --> 00:25:19,747
Everyone on set
had nothing but praise for her.

408
00:25:19,772 --> 00:25:21,728
I really can't wait
for everyone to see her.

409
00:25:21,799 --> 00:25:24,251
And keep an eye on
Cartoon's outfits too.

410
00:25:24,276 --> 00:25:30,425
Every outfit has its own little
details and a unique design.

411
00:25:30,450 --> 00:25:36,392
Miss Nana also gets to design
some of the outfits herself.

412
00:25:36,417 --> 00:25:40,156
And for those outfits,
we partnered with

413
00:25:40,181 --> 00:25:44,256
a wonderful designer specializing
in Thai textile patterns.

414
00:25:44,281 --> 00:25:47,244
And Miss Nana turns
those patterns into an outfit.

415
00:25:47,269 --> 00:25:50,413
What it looks like, you'll have
to watch the series to find out.

416
00:25:50,438 --> 00:25:52,159
But trust me, it's really cool.

417
00:25:52,184 --> 00:25:58,063
And we're hoping to bring
that outfit to life too.

418
00:25:58,197 --> 00:26:01,984
So please stay tuned,
and let us know what you think.

419
00:26:02,009 --> 00:26:04,786
If you guys love it,
we might actually make it!

420
00:26:04,881 --> 00:26:08,082
Cartoon is
a very open-minded actor.

421
00:26:08,107 --> 00:26:10,925
It was really easy
to work with her

422
00:26:10,950 --> 00:26:15,591
and adjust her approach
to fit this character.

423
00:26:15,616 --> 00:26:17,044
She really
tried to understand her,

424
00:26:17,069 --> 00:26:19,516
and she'd do her own homework
and come to us with ideas like,

425
00:26:19,541 --> 00:26:20,810
"Would it help if I did this?

426
00:26:20,835 --> 00:26:24,905
Would that make the character
come across more clearly?

427
00:26:24,930 --> 00:26:26,862
Is this how she would think?"

428
00:26:26,887 --> 00:26:28,771
She was constantly
giving us feedback.

429
00:26:28,796 --> 00:26:31,669
Whenever she rehearsed,
she'd come back and say,

430
00:26:31,694 --> 00:26:34,815
"I've done my homework,
what if we did it like this?"

431
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:36,276
She contributed so much.

432
00:26:36,301 --> 00:26:38,278
You'll see this really
cute side of Cartoon

433
00:26:38,303 --> 00:26:40,430
where she's not worried
about looking silly.

434
00:26:40,455 --> 00:26:43,436
She never lets
even the smallest detail slip by.

435
00:26:43,461 --> 00:26:47,456
Even in tiny moments, she makes
every little beat count.

436
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:51,341
That's something I really admire
about her performance.

437
00:26:51,394 --> 00:26:54,692
Working with Ing?
I'd say the word is "trust."

438
00:26:54,717 --> 00:26:57,353
We've done
so many scenes together,

439
00:26:57,378 --> 00:26:58,888
and there are times
when we're like,

440
00:26:58,913 --> 00:27:01,056
"It's so hot. We're exhausted.
We're soaked.

441
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:02,733
There's just so much going on."

442
00:27:02,765 --> 00:27:04,623
Everything can get
really exhausting,

443
00:27:04,648 --> 00:27:06,551
but we still give it our all.

444
00:27:06,575 --> 00:27:07,824
And when I turn to her,

445
00:27:07,849 --> 00:27:09,969
I'd look at her and see
she was still going all out.

446
00:27:09,994 --> 00:27:12,253
Neither of us ever gets tired
to the point of giving up.

447
00:27:12,278 --> 00:27:14,164
It feels like
we're in it together,

448
00:27:14,189 --> 00:27:17,202
like, "We'll get through
this scene together, Ing."

449
00:27:17,512 --> 00:27:19,749
Even when we're like,
"I just wanna go home!"

450
00:27:20,409 --> 00:27:22,670
I'd look at her and think,

451
00:27:22,694 --> 00:27:25,005
"Okay,
she's still in this with me."

452
00:27:40,277 --> 00:27:42,821
Minagi is naturally very cool.

453
00:27:42,846 --> 00:27:45,291
From her personality
and the way she carries herself,

454
00:27:45,331 --> 00:27:48,553
I thought
she'd make a great golf pro,

455
00:27:48,578 --> 00:27:52,006
which is exactly
what Pro Jin is in the series.

456
00:27:52,031 --> 00:27:55,904
With her personality
and her look,

457
00:27:55,929 --> 00:27:58,014
she has
such a distinctive presence.

458
00:27:58,038 --> 00:28:00,606
The moment you see her,
you immediately know,

459
00:28:00,631 --> 00:28:02,161
"That's Pro Jin."

460
00:28:02,185 --> 00:28:06,251
She's actually
a pretty quiet person by nature,

461
00:28:06,276 --> 00:28:09,329
both on set and in everyday life.

462
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:13,398
So sometimes
when we're about to shoot

463
00:28:13,423 --> 00:28:16,232
we have to
bring her energy up a little,

464
00:28:16,257 --> 00:28:19,289
like, "Come on, give us more!"

465
00:28:19,314 --> 00:28:21,653
And she can do it.

466
00:28:21,678 --> 00:28:24,028
She gives us exactly
what we're looking for.

467
00:28:24,053 --> 00:28:26,010
So she did a great job.

468
00:28:26,035 --> 00:28:29,050
We were also lucky with Minagi

469
00:28:29,075 --> 00:28:31,235
because she's been learning golf
since she was little.

470
00:28:31,259 --> 00:28:34,112
She loves the sport and still
goes out and plays regularly.

471
00:28:34,137 --> 00:28:39,887
We wanted another golf pro
who felt different from Pro Vee.

472
00:28:39,912 --> 00:28:41,603
Someone quiet and reserved,

473
00:28:41,628 --> 00:28:44,876
who seems to be carrying
something from her past.

474
00:28:44,901 --> 00:28:47,283
Next up is Bam.

475
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:51,722
She looks amazing
in every single outfit she wears.

476
00:28:51,747 --> 00:28:54,622
This is actually
Bam's first acting role.

477
00:28:54,647 --> 00:28:56,945
She had no acting experience
before this,

478
00:28:56,970 --> 00:28:58,453
but she did incredibly well.

479
00:28:58,477 --> 00:29:02,105
She could get through pages
and pages of dialogue smoothly,

480
00:29:02,130 --> 00:29:03,519
and she did it really well.

481
00:29:03,673 --> 00:29:06,722
She was great
with her expressions

482
00:29:06,747 --> 00:29:09,651
and playing off
her scene partners.

483
00:29:09,676 --> 00:29:11,237
Everyone was very happy with her.

484
00:29:11,262 --> 00:29:13,896
Both in real life
and in the series,

485
00:29:13,921 --> 00:29:18,421
Belle, the secretary,
is bright and cheerful.

486
00:29:18,446 --> 00:29:23,098
She's super chatty.
She can just talk and talk.

487
00:29:23,123 --> 00:29:27,189
That's Belle's character too.
She's always talking...

488
00:29:27,214 --> 00:29:29,813
And she's pretty talkative
in real life too.

489
00:29:29,838 --> 00:29:33,125
Belle is a very bright,
bubbly character.

490
00:29:33,150 --> 00:29:34,658
But underneath all that,

491
00:29:34,683 --> 00:29:38,668
there's a sensitive, vulnerable,
and more serious side to her.

492
00:29:38,693 --> 00:29:41,273
And that actually
surprised us too.

493
00:29:41,298 --> 00:29:43,322
We were like, "Oh, Bam has
this side to her too."

494
00:29:43,347 --> 00:29:45,651
When she brought out
a side of herself,

495
00:29:45,676 --> 00:29:47,792
beyond her usual
bubbly personality,

496
00:29:47,816 --> 00:29:52,685
we realized Bam is definitely
an actor to keep an eye on.

497
00:29:52,710 --> 00:29:54,363
She's really got something.

498
00:29:54,506 --> 00:29:57,886
Aren't you going to ask me
about golf or my experience?

499
00:29:57,924 --> 00:30:01,755
No. I've already done my research
on you, Pro Jin.

500
00:30:01,780 --> 00:30:03,357
I have no doubts about you.

501
00:30:03,587 --> 00:30:05,264
Can you start tomorrow?

502
00:30:06,081 --> 00:30:07,121
Tomorrow?

503
00:30:11,921 --> 00:30:16,910
She's really easygoing
and laid-back.

504
00:30:16,935 --> 00:30:18,711
She doesn't get too stressed.

505
00:30:18,736 --> 00:30:23,214
Whenever I talked to her,
she'd always put me at ease.

506
00:30:23,239 --> 00:30:26,105
So doing scenes together
felt really easy.

507
00:30:26,130 --> 00:30:28,871
She may seem really introverted,

508
00:30:28,896 --> 00:30:30,952
but whenever I need to talk
about something,

509
00:30:30,977 --> 00:30:33,354
she's a really good listener.

510
00:30:33,379 --> 00:30:35,918
So I felt really comfortable

511
00:30:35,943 --> 00:30:38,860
talking to her
about different scenes.

512
00:30:38,885 --> 00:30:41,582
Sometimes I'll ask her,
"Did I do okay?"

513
00:30:41,607 --> 00:30:43,434
And she's always there
to encourage me.

514
00:30:43,459 --> 00:30:45,757
We're always
encouraging each other.

515
00:30:54,165 --> 00:30:55,951
From the very beginning,

516
00:30:55,976 --> 00:30:59,922
our team paid close attention
to every detail,

517
00:30:59,947 --> 00:31:03,797
starting with casting
and script development.

518
00:31:03,822 --> 00:31:07,385
We did a lot of research on golf
and golf courses

519
00:31:07,410 --> 00:31:09,864
to make sure the script
was as well-informed as possible.

520
00:31:09,889 --> 00:31:12,485
Like I said,
we did a lot of outdoor shooting.

521
00:31:12,510 --> 00:31:16,187
so the lighting and camera crews
really gave it their all.

522
00:31:16,212 --> 00:31:18,595
Rain or whatever came our way,

523
00:31:18,620 --> 00:31:21,984
everyone did their best
to make sure we got through it.

524
00:31:22,009 --> 00:31:26,718
On set, we'd have over a hundred
crew members working out.

525
00:31:26,743 --> 00:31:30,049
And as you can see, a golf course
is huge and wide open.

526
00:31:30,074 --> 00:31:33,946
It was hard to control
all the different elements,

527
00:31:33,971 --> 00:31:36,321
so every scene took
a lot of work from everyone.

528
00:31:36,346 --> 00:31:38,438
There were hundreds of people
out on the course,

529
00:31:38,462 --> 00:31:40,814
with scaffolding, cranes,
everything.

530
00:31:40,839 --> 00:31:42,690
Every department worked together

531
00:31:42,715 --> 00:31:46,001
to get the best possible shots
to tell this story.

532
00:31:46,026 --> 00:31:49,862
Behind the scenes,
it took a huge crew

533
00:31:49,942 --> 00:31:54,597
just to set up the cameras
and shoot each scene.

534
00:31:54,622 --> 00:31:57,271
If you ever see
the behind-the-scenes footage,

535
00:31:57,296 --> 00:32:00,228
there might be only one
or two actors in the actual shot,

536
00:32:00,247 --> 00:32:02,009
but behind the camera,

537
00:32:02,033 --> 00:32:05,022
there are ten, twenty,
even thirty people!

538
00:32:36,094 --> 00:32:40,592
I get all giddy
watching both couples.

539
00:32:40,650 --> 00:32:43,738
With Ing and Cartoon,
for example,

540
00:32:43,894 --> 00:32:47,561
even now,
whether I'm reading the script,

541
00:32:47,704 --> 00:32:49,699
filming, or even editing...

542
00:32:50,009 --> 00:32:54,276
I've seen these scenes
so many times,

543
00:32:54,585 --> 00:32:58,270
and I never get tired of them.

544
00:32:58,295 --> 00:33:02,727
Every single time,
I still blush and smile.

545
00:33:02,752 --> 00:33:06,511
It's the same
with Pro Jin and Belle.

546
00:33:06,536 --> 00:33:09,490
Those two make me blush
just as much.

547
00:33:09,515 --> 00:33:12,285
You'll have to watch
and see for yourselves.

548
00:33:12,382 --> 00:33:15,925
Ing and Cartoon have this sweet,
innocent kind of chemistry.

549
00:33:15,950 --> 00:33:18,741
We'd be watching and wondering,

550
00:33:18,766 --> 00:33:21,333
"How far will Cartoon
take the intimacy in this scene?"

551
00:33:21,358 --> 00:33:23,105
And then she'd surprise us.

552
00:33:34,386 --> 00:33:37,637
Minagi and Bam are the same,
but with a different dynamic.

553
00:33:37,662 --> 00:33:40,364
The second couple
is a lot spicier.

554
00:33:40,389 --> 00:33:43,097
And wow,
when Bam really goes for it

555
00:33:43,122 --> 00:33:47,981
in those physical,
intimate scenes, she goes all in.

556
00:33:48,006 --> 00:33:50,824
And Minagi gives it right back.

557
00:33:50,849 --> 00:33:52,408
Whatever Bam throws at her,

558
00:33:52,433 --> 00:33:54,210
Minagi takes it
and fires right back.

559
00:33:54,234 --> 00:33:58,264
There's this emotional
push and pull,

560
00:33:58,289 --> 00:34:01,269
with all the flirting
back and forth.

561
00:34:01,294 --> 00:34:04,906
It's almost like watching them
play a game,

562
00:34:04,931 --> 00:34:07,218
waiting to see who'll win
and who'll give in first.

563
00:34:16,043 --> 00:34:21,953
I'm really glad
I got to play Pro Jin.

564
00:34:21,978 --> 00:34:27,351
I got to explore
new feelings and emotions,

565
00:34:27,376 --> 00:34:29,225
even what it's like
to stand up for myself.

566
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:32,333
Because in real life, I'd never
confront people the way she does.

567
00:34:32,358 --> 00:34:34,350
I really like this character,

568
00:34:34,375 --> 00:34:37,702
and I'm glad I got the chance
to step into her shoes.

569
00:34:37,727 --> 00:34:39,640
As for whether it's true

570
00:34:39,664 --> 00:34:42,364
that I said I didn't want to
do comedy... yes.

571
00:34:42,823 --> 00:34:44,733
Well, it's not that
I don't want to do comedy.

572
00:34:44,758 --> 00:34:47,195
It's just that
with my personality,

573
00:34:47,220 --> 00:34:49,863
I keep getting cast
in these cute,

574
00:34:49,888 --> 00:34:52,803
bubbly, slightly goofy roles.

575
00:34:52,828 --> 00:34:56,026
And to be fair,
that is kind of like me.

576
00:34:56,051 --> 00:34:58,904
But I wanted to try showing
a different side of myself.

577
00:34:58,929 --> 00:35:01,969
I wanted to try acting
all cool like Pro Vee.

578
00:35:01,994 --> 00:35:03,994
But I guess comedy
is just my calling.

579
00:35:04,242 --> 00:35:06,217
Maybe that's where
I'm really gonna shine!

580
00:35:06,536 --> 00:35:08,753
There were so many scenes

581
00:35:08,778 --> 00:35:11,578
where I had to keep
a straight face and just listen.

582
00:35:11,889 --> 00:35:14,103
And the second they called cut,
I'd turn to Bank and go,

583
00:35:14,128 --> 00:35:16,431
"Ugh, this is killing me!
I wanna talk!"

584
00:35:16,456 --> 00:35:18,141
I did that so many times.

585
00:35:18,166 --> 00:35:20,309
But later on,
Pro Vee does start talking more.

586
00:35:20,334 --> 00:35:23,664
You get to see her as this sweet,
caring big-sister type.

587
00:35:24,030 --> 00:35:26,799
We also have child actors

588
00:35:26,824 --> 00:35:29,633
playing Pro Vee and Nana
when they were little.

589
00:35:29,666 --> 00:35:33,901
They've known each other since
they were kids, like sisters.

590
00:35:34,114 --> 00:35:36,629
Vee and Nana, just like that.

591
00:35:36,654 --> 00:35:39,615
And the two of them were
absolutely adorable together.

592
00:35:39,649 --> 00:35:43,264
One had acting experience
and the other didn't,

593
00:35:43,289 --> 00:35:47,083
but they were both determined
to make it work.

594
00:35:47,108 --> 00:35:49,205
And they did such a great job.

595
00:35:49,230 --> 00:35:51,408
That's another part
I can't wait for everyone to see.

596
00:36:05,669 --> 00:36:09,613
We're so happy
to have such well-known,

597
00:36:09,638 --> 00:36:15,113
experienced actors join us.

598
00:36:15,138 --> 00:36:17,498
We have Tai Penpak,

599
00:36:17,523 --> 00:36:21,215
and Am Amarin,
who's a huge golf guy himself.

600
00:36:21,240 --> 00:36:22,940
He even has his own golf show.

601
00:36:22,965 --> 00:36:27,173
We also have Looknam Pamela,
who had to be paired with Am.

602
00:36:27,198 --> 00:36:29,661
We're so happy
to have her with us too.

603
00:36:29,686 --> 00:36:33,447
And Ouan Rangsit
also joined us for the series.

604
00:36:33,646 --> 00:36:35,697
And of course, Pingpong!

605
00:36:35,730 --> 00:36:40,074
She joined the cast and brought
so much fun to the set.

606
00:36:40,107 --> 00:36:44,622
We also have Talay,
who is seriously so handsome,

607
00:36:44,798 --> 00:36:49,453
but he plays
such a convincing villain.

608
00:37:32,575 --> 00:37:36,027
(What would you do
in this situation?)

609
00:37:36,052 --> 00:37:38,620
(If you heard a strange noise
at night, who'd go check it out?)

610
00:37:38,645 --> 00:37:40,104
I can answer that.
We'd go together.

611
00:37:40,129 --> 00:37:42,098
Because Pro Vee
is a scaredy-cat too!

612
00:37:42,123 --> 00:37:43,264
Exactly.

613
00:37:43,289 --> 00:37:47,151
This is actually based on
one of our scenes.

614
00:37:47,176 --> 00:37:49,262
- There's this one scene where...
- We'd go together.

615
00:37:49,287 --> 00:37:51,005
But Pro Vee's like
one millimeter ahead.

616
00:37:51,030 --> 00:37:54,523
We'd be one behind the other,
but still going together.

617
00:37:54,567 --> 00:37:55,908
And... action!

618
00:38:06,889 --> 00:38:09,087
(They look terrified.)

619
00:38:09,112 --> 00:38:12,257
I'd probably go check, while
Belle would just keep sleeping.

620
00:38:12,633 --> 00:38:13,863
I'd go with you.

621
00:38:15,329 --> 00:38:17,970
- Aren't you gonna wake her up?
- Oh! Right, wake her up.

622
00:38:18,493 --> 00:38:20,874
I'd check first
to make sure it's safe.

623
00:38:20,950 --> 00:38:23,060
Then if there's actually
something, I'd wake her up.

624
00:38:23,085 --> 00:38:24,853
If not, I'll let her sleep.
(So sweet!)

625
00:38:24,878 --> 00:38:27,719
Wait, you'd only wake me
if there was something? What for?

626
00:38:27,744 --> 00:38:28,903
To run!

627
00:38:28,928 --> 00:38:30,728
(Lost in the woods
with one banana leaf,

628
00:38:30,753 --> 00:38:31,770
who would give it up?)

629
00:38:31,795 --> 00:38:33,691
Would a banana leaf
even help, though?

630
00:38:34,553 --> 00:38:35,989
I think we'd just cuddle.

631
00:38:37,502 --> 00:38:38,723
- We'd just cuddle.
- Yeah.

632
00:38:38,748 --> 00:38:41,159
Seriously, would a banana leaf
even keep you warm?

633
00:38:41,334 --> 00:38:42,691
Maybe it'd cover, like...

634
00:38:42,716 --> 00:38:44,824
Yeah, let's just cuddle.
That'd probably be warmer.

635
00:38:45,105 --> 00:38:47,614
We could cuddle
under it and share.

636
00:38:47,639 --> 00:38:49,075
Half and half.

637
00:38:50,943 --> 00:38:52,760
- Sneaky!
- Sneaky...

638
00:38:52,977 --> 00:38:55,780
(If you got lost in the woods,
who would freak out first?)

639
00:38:55,804 --> 00:38:57,805
- Nana.
- Definitely Nana.

640
00:38:57,830 --> 00:39:00,090
Pro Vee would have to be
the one going, "Calm down."

641
00:39:00,115 --> 00:39:03,321
Pro Vee would be more stern,
not like, "Aww, calm down."

642
00:39:03,354 --> 00:39:05,369
It'd be more like,
"Why are you crying?

643
00:39:05,394 --> 00:39:07,531
What's wrong?
Pull yourself together!"

644
00:39:07,556 --> 00:39:10,366
- She'd definitely lose it first.
- Very possible.

645
00:39:10,467 --> 00:39:12,981
Yeah, if I really reached
my breaking point.

646
00:39:13,006 --> 00:39:16,010
And then she'd be the one
who comes over to comfort me.

647
00:39:16,471 --> 00:39:17,527
Go on, comfort her.

648
00:39:23,647 --> 00:39:26,180
Not sure
if that's calming her down

649
00:39:26,205 --> 00:39:28,308
or getting her
even more worked up.

650
00:40:06,006 --> 00:40:10,486
Everyone, make sure you tune in
to our series, Fairway of Love!

651
00:40:10,511 --> 00:40:14,070
I promise it'll be a lot of fun,
just like we've been saying.

652
00:40:14,095 --> 00:40:17,471
We're bringing you golf
in a fun and entertaining way.

653
00:40:17,496 --> 00:40:21,379
You'll get to discover golf
alongside our Nana here,

654
00:40:21,404 --> 00:40:24,479
with Pro Vee right here
to teach her along the way.

655
00:40:24,504 --> 00:40:26,752
And besides all the fun
around golf,

656
00:40:26,777 --> 00:40:29,272
there's also the relationship
between the two of us.

657
00:40:29,297 --> 00:40:32,264
How will someone
who acts all cool

658
00:40:32,289 --> 00:40:34,002
click with someone
this bright and bubbly?

659
00:40:34,027 --> 00:40:36,799
You'll have to watch and see.

660
00:40:37,270 --> 00:40:39,384
And please look forward
to Pro Jin too.

661
00:40:39,409 --> 00:40:43,545
You'll have to wait and see
what Pro Jin goes through,

662
00:40:43,570 --> 00:40:46,072
what choices she'll have to make,
and where they lead her.

663
00:40:46,097 --> 00:40:49,774
And you probably don't even know
yet how we fell in love.

664
00:40:49,799 --> 00:40:51,784
- In the series.
- In the series!

665
00:40:51,809 --> 00:40:54,776
And I hope you'll look forward
to Belle too.

666
00:40:54,801 --> 00:40:58,157
I put so much
into this character,

667
00:40:58,182 --> 00:41:00,834
- since it's my first project.
- Our first project!

668
00:41:00,859 --> 00:41:03,590
We hope everyone gets to enjoy
all the sweet moments

669
00:41:03,615 --> 00:41:06,082
and learn a little
about golf along the way.

670
00:41:06,107 --> 00:41:09,777
And our series really has
a little bit of everything.

671
00:41:09,802 --> 00:41:11,557
Bitter, sour, sweet, salty.
You name it!

672
00:41:11,582 --> 00:41:14,108
And most importantly, it's hot,
spicy, and full of sparks!

673
00:41:14,133 --> 00:41:16,276
- We've got it all.
- Oh, yeah. Especially us!

674
00:41:16,301 --> 00:41:20,701
If you want to see the two of us
in Fairway of Love,

675
00:41:20,726 --> 00:41:23,950
tune in this September!

676
00:41:23,975 --> 00:41:27,383
- On One31, and also...
- WeTV!

677
00:41:27,408 --> 00:41:31,094
Please show lots of love
to Fairway of Love.

678
00:41:31,119 --> 00:41:33,119
- We hope you'll tune in!
- Bye-bye!
